</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="state" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Bit address state indicator for certain more limited HMIs]]>
</Description>
<Comments>
<Comment Operand=".0">
<![CDATA[running]]>
</Comment>
<Comment Operand=".1">
<![CDATA[complete]]>
</Comment>
<Comment Operand=".2">
<![CDATA[pausing]]>
</Comment>
<Comment Operand=".3">
<![CDATA[paused]]>
</Comment>
<Comment Operand=".4">
<![CDATA[restarting]]>
</Comment>
<Comment Operand=".5">
<![CDATA[aborting]]>
</Comment>
<Comment Operand=".6">
<![CDATA[aborted]]>
</Comment>
</Comments>
<DefaultData Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[0]]>
</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="startupStep" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Step which sequence will init to on first scan. Defaults to aborted]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[7000]]>
</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="7000"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="internalOns" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<DefaultData Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[0]]>
</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="hmiModeSel" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<DefaultData Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[0]]>
</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="watchdog" DataType="TIMER" ExternalAccess="None">
<DefaultData Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[0,0,0]]]>
</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="TIMER">
<DataValueMember Name="PRE" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="ACC" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="TT" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="DN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="stateUpdated" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<DefaultData Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[0]]>
</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[SeqCtrl: Handles the basic logic for state transitions and HMI handling for sequences. 

To Use:
	- Place on a rung that runs every scan BEFORE any of the steps
	- Map/set the mode input to True (1) to disable HMI control. 
	- Map/Set the disableHmiStart input to True (1) to disable the HMI start button, typically for when the safety system is not in a safe state.

Sequences, written externally, should always be interacted with by using the following inputs:
- cmdStart
- cmdAbort
- cmdPause
- nextStep

NEVER write directly to currentStep.

See AIC Wiki for more details]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Change the startup step on first scan/power on
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(S:FS)MOVE(startupStep,currentStep)MOVE(startupStep,nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Use a bool and jump label to updated the state (running/aborted/etc) bits twice. 
- Once here at the beginning before we check what commands are valid, and 
- a second time at the end once the step has been updated]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(stateUpdated)JMP(updateState);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(begin)NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Set the current "mode"
need to have a pseudo-automode when running code so that IO will respond, but system is not in full running/automode]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(mode)XIO(autoModeOverride)OTE(hmiModeSel);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   HMI Button Handling   /////////

When valid, set the corresponding PLC command(s) when the HMI requests it. HMI should Set On the commands (once) and this program will turn them off.

Start Button]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(hmiCmdStart)ONS(internalOns.1)[XIO(hmiModeSel) XIO(disableHmiStart) OTL(cmdStart) OTL(autoModeOverride) ,OTU(hmiCmdStart) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Start Button Visibility]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(hmiModeSel)XIO(disableHmiStart)[XIC(complete) ,XIC(paused) ,XIC(aborted) ]OTE(hmiStartVisible);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Abort]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(hmiCmdAbort)ONS(internalOns.2)[XIO(hmiModeSel) OTL(cmdAbort) OTL(autoModeOverride) ,OTU(hmiCmdAbort) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Abort Button Visibility]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(hmiModeSel)XIO(complete)XIO(aborted)OTE(hmiAbortVisible);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Pause (Hold)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(hmiCmdPause)ONS(internalOns.4)[XIO(hmiModeSel) OTL(cmdPause) OTL(autoModeOverride) ,OTU(hmiCmdPause) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Hold Button Visibility]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(hmiModeSel)[XIC(running) ,XIC(pausing) ,XIC(restarting) ]OTE(hmiPauseVisible);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset AutoMode Override]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(aborted) ONS(internalOns.7) ,XIC(complete) ONS(internalOns.8) ,XIC(paused) ONS(internalOns.9) ]OTU(autoModeOverride);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[In Active State: a shortcut to check if the sequence is running code vs is in and idle state]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(running) ,XIC(pausing) ,XIC(restarting) ,XIC(aborting) ]OTE(inAnActiveState);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Reject Invalid CMDs   /////////

Prevents random bits from getting latched on and causing unexpected execution


]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdAbort)[XIC(complete) ,XIC(aborting) ,XIC(aborted) ]OTU(cmdAbort)OTU(autoModeOverride);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdStart)XIO(complete)XIO(aborted)XIO(paused)OTU(cmdStart)OTU(autoModeOverride);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdPause)XIO(running)XIO(restarting)OTU(cmdPause)OTU(autoModeOverride);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Parse Commands and Transition States   //////////

Any state transition that requires a command should be handled here. Exceptions are:
- going from running to complete
- going from pausing to paused
- going from aborting to aborted

Respond to start command. Varies based on state]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdStart)[[XIC(complete) ,XIC(aborted) ] MOVE(0,nextStep) ,XIC(paused) MOVE(5000,nextStep) ,OTU(cmdStart) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Respond to pause command

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdPause)[MOVE(3000,nextStep) ,ONS(internalOns.13) [MOVE(currentStep,stepBeforePause) ,XIC(running) MOVE(currentStep,runningStepBeforePause) ] ,OTU(cmdPause) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
Respond to Abort Command

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdAbort)[MOVE(6000,nextStep) ,ONS(internalOns.12) MOVE(currentStep,stepBeforeAbort) ,OTU(cmdAbort) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Step Control   /////////

Enable autoStep to run code normally
Disable autoStep and manually toggle singleStep for control of sequence execution

NOTE: This should be last rung of any sort of step control logic so that all parsing and checks of commands happen before the step number acutally changes.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(autoStep) ,XIC(singleStep) ][MOVE(nextStep,currentStep) ,OTU(singleStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(updateState)NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Set Status Bits   /////////


Running Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIMIT(0,currentStep,1999)OTE(running);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Complete Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(currentStep,2000)OTE(complete);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Pausing Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIMIT(3000,currentStep,3999)OTE(pausing);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Paused Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(currentStep,4000)OTE(paused);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Restarting Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIMIT(5000,currentStep,5999)OTE(restarting);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Aborting Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIMIT(6000,currentStep,6999)OTE(aborting);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Aborted Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(currentStep,7000)OTE(aborted);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Use stateUpdated bit to call this chunk of code twice. Once at the beginning in case someone messed with currentStep and then at the end in normal order to reflect what changed]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(stateUpdated)OTL(stateUpdated)JMP(begin);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(stateUpdated);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Faulted Status   /////////

Set faulted status bit if any fault bit is set on]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NE(fault,0)OTE(faulted);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Create a bit addressed state output for HMIs with limited functionality (like C-More or View Studio)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(running)OTE(state.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(complete)OTE(state.1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(pausing)OTE(state.2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(paused)OTE(state.3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(restarting)OTE(state.4);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(aborting)OTE(state.5);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(aborted)OTE(state.6);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
<Programs Use="Context">
<Program Use="Context" Name="MainProgram">
<Tags Use="Context">
<Tag Name="sequence" TagType="Base" DataType="SeqCtrl" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[33558535,7000,7000,0,0,5000,0,0,64,7000,128,[0,2000,0]]]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="SeqCtrl">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="mode" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="autoModeOverride" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="disableHmiStart" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="faulted" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="running" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="complete" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="pausing" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="paused" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="restarting" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="aborting" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="aborted" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="inAnActiveState" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="cmdStart" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="cmdPause" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="cmdAbort" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="autoStep" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="singleStep" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiCmdStart" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiCmdPause" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiCmdAbort" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiStartVisible" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiPauseVisible" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiAbortVisible" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="currentStep" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="7000"/>
<DataValueMember Name="nextStep" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="7000"/>
<DataValueMember Name="fault" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="ons" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="stepBeforeAbort" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="5000"/>
<DataValueMember Name="stepBeforePause" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="runningStepBeforePause" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="state" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="64"/>
<DataValueMember Name="startupStep" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="7000"/>
</Structure>
</Data>
</Tag>
</Tags>
<Routines Use="Context">
<Routine Use="Target" Name="SequenceRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Sequence V3.0

Please note that this version is dramatically different than previous versions of Sequences. Please consult the below comments and the AIC Wiki for more details.

AIC's default Finite State Machine based loosely on the AB Equipment Phase.
One Shot (ONS) and Latch On (OTL) the command bits (sequence.cmd___) to change states. The sequence controller will unlatch bits when done and signal once it has reached a new state.

<Comments enclosed in brackets intended to be deleted. These comments are mostly a "tutorial" for how to start with this routine. The "clean" version of this routine exludes all tutorial type comments and the stats AOI. The clean version is likely easier to import and use once you are used to this program structure/interface.>

Step Numbering Scheme
-------------------------
Running: 0-1999
Complete: 2000
Pausing: 3000-3999
Paused: 4000
Restarting (Resume from Paused): 5000-5999
Aborting: 6000-6999
Aborted: 7000

<Optional: Delete this rung when done reading>

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[//////////   Prescan   /////////

<
Put code that runs before the sequence here
This is also a good spot for code related to this sequence that runs all the time
Also also this is a good spot to put logic for when to abort or pause, say if your safety trips. Note, DO NOT set the step number manually. ALWAYS use the sequence.cmd___ bits
>]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Sequence Status and Control   /////////

<
Note: the "mode" should typically be connected to the system mode (1/True for Auto)
"disableHmiStart" should typically be linked to safety such that an Estop disables starting the program
Alternatively, the signals can be left as is to always enable PLC and HMI control of this program regradless of mode or safety or whatever else

For step control:
Enable autoStep to run code normally (auto increment steps)
Disable autoStep and manually toggle singleStep for control of sequence step increments
>
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SeqCtrl(sequence,1,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Running   /////////

Steps 0 - 1999

<
Set On the cmdStart bit to reach this step from complete, aborted, or paused

Put your code to do stuff here. Spread out steps so intermediate steps can be added later. 
Always start a step with EQU(seq.currentStep, <some number>) and always end with MOV(<some number>, seq.nextStep)
NEVER write directly to seq.currentStep

Typically, sequences should start with resetting anything needed to run correctly, and then run whatever sequences is required

Go to Complete (Step 2000) when done running or reloop back to an earlier step to run forever
>]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(sequence.currentStep,0)MOVE(2000,sequence.nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   COMPLETE   /////////

Step 2000. Done. Waiting for start command to go back to beginning of running. 
Step transition handled by SeqCtrl AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Pausing (Holding)   /////////

<
Set on the cmdPause bit when running to reach this point.

OPTIONAL: Stop anything that needs to stop before pausing. SeqCtrl will log what the running step was before pausing. Go to paused (step 4000) when done.
If Pausing/Paused/Restart is not needed, DELETE these steps and disable the Pause button on the HMI.
>]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(sequence.currentStep,3000)MOVE(4000,sequence.nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Paused  /////////

OPTIONAL
Step 4000. Program paused/held in place. Waiting for start to go resume running where it left off
Step transition handled by SeqCtrl AOI

<If Pausing/Paused/Restart is not needed, DELETE these steps and disable the Pause button on the HMI>]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Restarting   /////////

<
Set on the cmdStart bit when paused to reach this point.

OPTIONAL: Reset and decide how to resume running, then return to where ever the program was before it was paused.
If Pausing/Paused/Restart is not needed, DELETE these steps and disable the Pause button on the HMI.
>]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(sequence.currentStep,5000)MOVE(sequence.runningStepBeforePause,sequence.nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   ABORTING   /////////

<
Set on the cmdAbort bit to reach this point
Stop some things and then go to aborted (step 7000) when done.
>]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(sequence.currentStep,6000)MOVE(7000,sequence.nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Aborted   /////////

Step 7000. Program Stopped/Canceled. Waiting for start to go back to beginning of running.
Step transition handled by SeqCtrl AOI]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
